<h1>about</h1>

<p>Hello, my name is Joe.</p>

<p>For as long as I can remember, I have had an interest in taking things apart, figuring out how they work, and putting them back together.
It started with Nerf guns as a kid, then grew into DIY electronics projects in high school, and then cars when I was old enough to drive.</p>

<p>Since I was born at a time when technology was less prevalent, I had a lot of interest in that as well.
But I did not like the idea of sitting behind a computer all day for a job. I enjoyed working with my hands too much.
</p>
<p>That's what makes my skills unique. Rebuilding a pump, troubleshooting a die set, replacing a motor? Sure.
Problems with automated equipment; PLC, sensors, solenoids? Sure.</p>

<h2>What I work on</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Automated equipment
    <ul>
    <li>Complete rehabilitation to fine tuning</li>
